reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${△,♢,♡},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(△,△)\\notin R,\\,(♢,♢)\\notin R,\\,(♡,♡)\\notin R.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$ $\\text{for all }x\\in A,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416844 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416845 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416846 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1069 "q-213244" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1071 "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\gamma }.$ Given that $R$ is reflexive, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix.\n\n|  | $\\alpha $ | $\\beta $ | $\\gamma $ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\alpha $ | {{field-1}} | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $\\beta $ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |\n| $\\gamma $ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1072 #uuid "08d898ff-f576-5e6a-bdf8-9d2e027a5e42" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416853 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be reflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(\\alpha ,\\alpha )\\in R,\\,(\\beta ,\\beta )\\in R,\\,(\\gamma ,\\gamma )\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis means that the diagonal elements of the adjacency matrix must all be $1,$