$ if and only if $(x+y)∣10,$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,S\\,y$ if and only if $4∣({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}),$ defined on $Z$\n\n- $x\\,T\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y+1),$ defined on $Z$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416858 1072 #uuid "7095468b-6aec-5ce6-83d1-ea12403a6b5a" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416858 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin R$ since $2+2=4$ and $4∤10,$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in R$ since $1+1=2$ and $2∣10.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is reflexive. Indeed, $(x,x)\\in S$ for all $x\\in Z.$ Notice that \n\n$$\n4∣({x}^{2}-{x}^{2})\n$$\n\nfor any $x\\in Z.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is neither reflexive nor irreflexive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,2)\\notin T$ since $2∤(2+1),$ while\n\n- $(1,1)\\in T$ since $1∣(1+1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\"" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416815 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416824 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416851 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1069 "q-213251" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1071 "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={5,8,10}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(5,5),(5,8),(8,10),(10,5),(10,8)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1072 #uuid "7c340422-8f3e-59cd-b595-ad2e94a755e0" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416859 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ de