reflexive nor irreflexive}.$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416816 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416834 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416836 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1069 "q-213202" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1071 "Let $R$ be a relation defined on the set $Z$ as follows: \n\n$\\,$ $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $2∤(y-x)$ \n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1072 #uuid "ccf91b35-7753-51f7-9fcf-6efffb54e68e" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416861 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nThe relation $R$ is irreflexive. Indeed, since $2∣(x-x)$ for all $x\\in Z,$ we have $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in Z.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$  $\\text{ for all }x\\in Z,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416817 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416820 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416828 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416831 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416839 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416842 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416843 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1069 "q-213245" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1071 "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={1,3,5,7}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(1,3),(1,5),(3,5),(5,7)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1072 #uuid "cfc59310-e932-539a-95d8-99d9f3c66e0d" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416862 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nIn our case, the relation is defined on ${1,3,5,7},$ and we have\n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R,\\,(5,5)\\notin R,\\,(7,7)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude the following:\n\n$\\,$ Since $(x,x)\\notin R$ $\\text{for all }x\\in A,$ the relation is $\\text{irreflexive}.$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1068 #edb/ref 17592186416823 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1069 "q-213228" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1071 "![](images/03/03ddf06402ad38708d232cf28783c817bf881965d54650eb158e7ffca4ea76a2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent irreflexive relations defined on the set $A={1,2,3}?$" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1072 #uuid "e1a27c07-b36b-5525-ba6b-847b13ebf516" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true] [17592186416863 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be irreflexive, we require \n\n$$\n(1,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,2)\\notin R,\\,(3,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/b6/b63d99459e8271e70ec36fd417d67565f3d5e77316815d49c235468e174aa1e9.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to an irreflexive relation must not contain diagonal points. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534271 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-003f486a-2600-584c-92ff-478adde52a81" 17592186416691 "answer-028f1dfa-86c2-5e3a-a73a-1d56a9225107" 17592186416692 "answer-0a759780-1d74-5387-9038-a0d11fb5f254" 17592186416693 "answer-0dc34d62-1b81-5d86-978c-763c5b1036fa" 17592186416694 "answer-0ed66ce8-a1ef-5ea8-befa-e99b6d7f0a0e" 17592186416695 "answer-0f2bcf16-6ee6-50d5-996d-c87fed6e4ab2" 17592186416696 "answer-104c8b41-ca6e-57c0-8d42-663c4bc18e77" 17592186416697 "answer-1332b1f3-7971-51f8-884d-3f0bb33c2169" 17592186416698 "answer-14634958-496e-54f5-b885-eeae73164e08" 17592186416699 "answer-15ff79dc-703d-570b-a9aa-b16ef1672f52" 17592186416700 "answer-172486d0-6c0d-50e4-abdb-4aeb9880c7ca" 17592186416701 "answer-174379d6-59e2-5ded-a704-513df037faa3" 17592186416702 "answer-17c1bb98-9a1e-56d2-af61-e483f5f7add1" 17592186416703 "answer-181aa40b-29c8-5d19-88a7-cb375283934d" 17592186416704 "answer-19832d4c-4f38-57f7-bb47-2e4d78cada0f" 17592186416705 "answer-1a41c584-e8f5-5ff9-a7e0-804b44214efb" 17592186416706 "answer-1a81e9c1-7c28-5079-bc82-6430dce1e7cf" 17592186416707 "answer-1ab03ed4-fb9b-5074-9880-fe1c53b1877b" 17592186416708 "answer-204ca137-4335-5470-825e-0717b79cf8e0" 17592186416709 "answer-2129ea14-351e-5487-85a4-c62570378b81" 17592186416710 "answer-21bdce35-1a6d-5b3f-a49e-4f39f1e7cd62" 17592186416711 "answer-24b4d9b2-5667-5784-aed1-24308c3938c3" 17592186416712 "answer-2e52c3bd-2b7a-5a24-95b6-a56a7a15447c" 17592186416713 "answer-306872e7-1d7b-5d08-a4d5-765ca66562d0" 17592186416714 "answer-34f96acd-fc2a-53e4-af03-f1157ecff40d" 17592186416715 "answer-36f3f0